Ask again for another site within the verifier's cache

The verifier keeps a person's approval for five seconds, so a browser's
preflight and its real request for one sign-in ask only once. It kept
the approval whatever was asked next, so a request from any other site,
or a registration, within those seconds was approved without asking.
Keep it only for the prompt that was approved, which names the
operation and the site.

